Pattern: Circuit Breaker

Purpose:
  Prevent cascading failures by tracking failure rates and
  opening circuits when thresholds are exceeded. Ensures system
  can fail fast and recover gracefully.

States:
  CLOSED:
    Normal operation. All requests pass through.
    Transition: -> OPEN after failure_threshold failures

  OPEN:
    Circuit is open. All requests fail immediately.
    Transition: -> HALF_OPEN after recovery_timeout

  HALF_OPEN:
    Limited requests allowed to test recovery.
    Transition: -> CLOSED after success_threshold successes
    Transition: -> OPEN after failure_threshold failures

Configuration:
  failure_threshold: 3
  recovery_timeout: 60s
  success_threshold: 2
  half_open_max_requests: 5

FailureDetection:
  Types: TIMEOUT, ERROR, VALIDATION, DEPENDENCY, RESOURCE
  Counting: consecutive failures tracked, reset on success

CircuitActions:
  Open:
    - Log circuit open event
    - Record failure reason
    - Notify human if stage is critical
    - Skip stage if non-critical
    - Update state: circuit_open

  HalfOpen:
    - Allow limited requests
    - Monitor success/failure
    - Close if success_threshold met
    - Re-open if failure_threshold met

  Close:
    - Log circuit close event
    - Reset failure counter
    - Resume normal operation

FallbackBehavior:
  On circuit open: skip stage, use cached result, or notify human
  On half-open: allow limited test requests
  On circuit close: resume normal operation

Monitoring:
  Metrics: circuit_state, failure_count, success_count, last_failure, last_success, recovery_attempts
  Alerts: circuit open -> notify human, half-open/close -> log

Rules:
  [CB1] Circuit MUST open after failure_threshold consecutive failures.
  [CB2] Circuit MUST transition to HALF_OPEN after recovery_timeout.
  [CB3] Circuit MUST close after success_threshold successes in HALF_OPEN.
  [CB4] Circuit MUST re-open if failure_threshold failures in HALF_OPEN.
  [CB5] Circuit state MUST be persisted for crash recovery.
  [CB6] Fallback MUST be defined for every protected stage.
  [CB7] Circuit breaker MUST NOT block critical human-initiated actions.

State: +